“Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform used to automate deployment, scaling, management, and networking of containerized applications.

“In production, Kubernetes helps achieve scalability, high availability, automation, and faster deployments with minimal downtime.”

Some major advantages of Kubernetes are:

1.High Availability
Kubernetes automatically distributes application replicas across nodes.
If one pod or node fails, Kubernetes recreates the pod automatically.

2.Auto Scaling
Using Horizontal Pod Autoscaler, Kubernetes can automatically increase or decrease pods based on CPU or memory usage.

3.Self-Healing
Kubernetes continuously monitors pod health.
If a container crashes, it restarts automatically.
If a node goes down, pods are rescheduled to another node.

4.Load Balancing & Service Discovery
Kubernetes provides built-in service discovery and load balancing using Services and Ingress.

5.Rolling Updates & Rollbacks
Applications can be updated with zero downtime using rolling updates.
If deployment fails, rollback can be done easily.

6.Efficient Resource Utilization
Kubernetes schedules workloads based on CPU and memory requests/limits, improving infrastructure utilization.

7.Portability
Applications can run on any cloud or on-premises environment like AWS EKS, Azure AKS, GKE, or bare metal.

8.Declarative Management
Infrastructure and applications are managed using YAML manifests, supporting Infrastructure as Code practices.

9.Security & Isolation
Kubernetes supports namespaces, RBAC, secrets, network policies, and pod security features.

10.Ecosystem & Integrations
It integrates easily with tools like:
Jenkins Helm Prometheus Grafana ArgoCD Istio Datadog
